<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<ContentDialog
    x:Class="Rudis.Shell.Dialogs.ExportDialog"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    FontFamily="Calibri"
    RequestedTheme="Dark"
    Background="{StaticResource bg-panel}"
    Foreground="{StaticResource text-primary}"
    BorderBrush="{StaticResource border-hairline}"
    BorderThickness="1"
    CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-panel}"
    AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog"
    AutomationProperties.Name="Export">

    <!--
      The v6.0 export dialog (frontend/index.html:645-695 `#export-dialog`), ported
      one-for-one into the C# shell as an IN-APP XAML MODAL.

      ═══ WHY A ContentDialog AND NOT A SHELL DIALOG ═══

      WinUI 3 renders a `ContentDialog` in its `XamlRoot`'s popup layer — the SAME
      visual tree as the `Preview` region's `SwapChainPanel`. That is the whole reason
      this exists: under the retired Tauri `SetWindowRgn` hole-punch the export dialog
      was one of THREE cases that stayed visually broken (research/v7-SUMMARY.md
      "Conflict 2"), because a WebView-drawn modal could not composite above a child
      HWND sitting at HWND_TOP. Here it is an ordinary sibling in one tree and simply
      works — there is no occluder rect, no region, and no window API anywhere in the
      shipped shell (mechanically gated, plan 51-01).

      A `FileSavePicker` (what the C# shell used before this plan) is a SHELL dialog
      in its own top-level window. It cannot overlap the panel and therefore proves
      nothing about layering — which is why v6.0's in-app modal is the thing being
      ported rather than kept as a picker.

      ═══ WHAT "Source" MEANS ═══

      `Source` is the ABSENCE of an override, not a fifth resolution: it maps to
      `null` and the caller falls back to `Toolbar.ResolveExportFormat()`'s existing
      mirrored-state derivation. The working behaviour is preserved as the DEFAULT
      rather than replaced.

      ═══ TOKENS ONLY ═══

      Every colour is a {StaticResource} token key from Theme/Tokens.xaml — a raw hex
      literal here is a build FAILURE (MechanicalGatesTests.
      no_raw_hex_outside_the_token_dictionary enumerates shell/Rudis.Shell/** for
      .cs and .xaml, so it covers this file the moment it exists). `RequestedTheme`
      is Dark so the stock ComboBox/TextBox chrome in the dialog's subtree matches
      the token palette instead of following the system light/dark setting.
    -->

    <ContentDialog.Resources>
        <!-- The stock ContentDialog template reads these keys. Aliasing them onto
             design tokens is how the surface, its hairline and its command area obey
             CLAUDE.md rule 7 without a single literal. -->
        <StaticResource x:Key="ContentDialogBackground" ResourceKey="bg-panel" />
        <StaticResource x:Key="ContentDialogForeground" ResourceKey="text-primary" />
        <StaticResource x:Key="ContentDialogBorderBrush" ResourceKey="border-hairline" />
        <StaticResource x:Key="ContentDialogTopOverlay" ResourceKey="bg-panel" />
        <StaticResource x:Key="ContentDialogSeparatorBorderBrush" ResourceKey="border-hairline" />

        <!-- Field label (handoff Typography: small, `text-secondary`). -->
        <Style x:Key="DialogFieldLabelStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-secondary}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,4" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Outlined (Cancel / Browse) — the same resolution Toolbar.xaml records
             for `ToolbarOutlinedButtonStyle`: outlined `border-strong`, hover fill
             `bg-elevated` (UI-SPEC gap 2). -->
        <Style x:Key="DialogOutlinedButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-primary}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{StaticResource border-strong}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource radius-control}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="14,0,14,0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualPrimaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualSecondaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource on-accent}" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Border x:Name="Fill"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-elevated}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-segment-active}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Label.Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-tertiary}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Label"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              FontWeight="{TemplateBinding FontWeight}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- Brand fill (the confirm action) — `accent` fill, `on-accent` text,
             hover `accent-bright`, exactly as Toolbar.ExportButton. -->
        <Style x:Key="DialogAccentButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{StaticResource accent}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource on-accent}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource radius-control}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="18,0,18,0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="30" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualPrimaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
            <Setter Property="FocusVisualSecondaryBrush" Value="{StaticResource on-accent}" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                        <Border x:Name="Fill"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                            <VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                                <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                                    <VisualState x:Name="PointerOver">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Pressed">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource accent-bright}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                    <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                                        <VisualState.Setters>
                                            <Setter Target="Fill.Background" Value="{StaticResource bg-elevated}" />
                                            <Setter Target="Label.Foreground" Value="{StaticResource text-tertiary}" />
                                        </VisualState.Setters>
                                    </VisualState>
                                </VisualStateGroup>
                            </VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups>
                            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Label"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                              FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                              FontWeight="{TemplateBinding FontWeight}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>
    </ContentDialog.Resources>

    <!-- The dialog's own surface Border. The ContentDialog template already paints
         `bg-panel`; this repeats it over the CONTENT area so the whole rectangle a
         layering capture crops to is one measurable colour rather than a mix of the
         template's padding and the content's transparency.

         ⚠ IT CARRIES ITS OWN AutomationId, and that is MEASURED rather than decorative.
         `ContentDialog`'s OWN automation peer reports the whole XamlRoot as its
         BoundingRectangle (a `window` peer spanning the popup root and its dimming
         layer) — plan 51-06's first run read {3822x1008} for a dialog roughly 500x550
         physical px, which made every occlusion reading a statement about the entire
         window. This Border is the dialog's real surface, so this is the element a
         layering proof must crop to. -->
    <Border Background="{StaticResource bg-panel}"
            Padding="20,18,20,18"
            CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-panel}"
            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Surface"
            AutomationProperties.Name="Export dialog surface"
            AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Content">
        <StackPanel Width="400" Spacing="14">

            <TextBlock Text="Export"
                       Foreground="{StaticResource text-primary}"
                       FontSize="17"
                       FontWeight="Bold" />

            <!-- Resolution — the option values are #export-dialog's, verbatim. -->
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="Resolution" Style="{StaticResource DialogFieldLabelStyle}" />
                <ComboBox x:Name="ResolutionBox"
                          HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                          SelectedIndex="0"
                          AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Resolution"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="Resolution">
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="">Source</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="1920x1080">1080p (1920×1080)</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="1280x720">720p (1280×720)</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="854x480">480p (854×480)</ComboBoxItem>
                </ComboBox>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- Frame rate. The item CONTENT is the bare number so the value the user
                 chose is the value the parser reads; the unit lives in the label. -->
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="Frame rate (fps)" Style="{StaticResource DialogFieldLabelStyle}" />
                <ComboBox x:Name="FpsBox"
                          HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                          SelectedIndex="0"
                          AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Fps"
                          AutomationProperties.Name="Frame rate">
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="">Source (match media)</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="24">24</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="25">25</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="30">30</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="60">60</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="80">80</ComboBoxItem>
                    <ComboBoxItem Tag="120">120</ComboBoxItem>
                </ComboBox>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- Folder + Browse… (v6's #export-dest / #export-browse). -->
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="Folder" Style="{StaticResource DialogFieldLabelStyle}" />
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBox x:Name="FolderBox"
                             Grid.Column="0"
                             PlaceholderText="Choose a folder…"
                             AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Folder"
                             AutomationProperties.Name="Export folder" />
                    <Button x:Name="BrowseButton"
                            Grid.Column="1"
                            Content="Browse…"
                            Style="{StaticResource DialogOutlinedButtonStyle}"
                            Click="OnBrowseClick"
                            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Browse"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Browse for export folder" />
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- File name + container (v6's #export-name / #export-format). -->
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="File name" Style="{StaticResource DialogFieldLabelStyle}" />
                <Grid ColumnSpacing="8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <TextBox x:Name="FileNameBox"
                             Grid.Column="0"
                             Text="rudis-export"
                             PlaceholderText="my-export"
                             AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Filename"
                             AutomationProperties.Name="Export file name" />
                    <ComboBox x:Name="FormatBox"
                              Grid.Column="1"
                              SelectedIndex="0"
                              AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Format"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Container">
                        <ComboBoxItem Tag=".mp4">.mp4</ComboBoxItem>
                        <ComboBoxItem Tag=".mov">.mov</ComboBoxItem>
                        <ComboBoxItem Tag=".mkv">.mkv</ComboBoxItem>
                    </ComboBox>
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- A refusal must be VISIBLE, never swallowed (50-05's rule, UI-SPEC §5).
                 No red/danger token exists in the handoff, so this uses the same
                 `text-secondary` on `bg-elevated` treatment Preview.ErrorState does. -->
            <Border x:Name="ErrorSurface"
                    Visibility="Collapsed"
                    Background="{StaticResource bg-elevated}"
                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource radius-control}"
                    Padding="10,8,10,8">
                <TextBlock x:Name="ErrorText"
                           Foreground="{StaticResource text-secondary}"
                           FontSize="12"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Error"
                           AutomationProperties.Name="Export dialog error" />
            </Border>

            <!-- ⚠ THE BUTTONS ARE THE DIALOG'S OWN, not ContentDialog's
                 PrimaryButton/CloseButton, and the reason is mechanical: those two
                 are TEMPLATE PARTS, so their AutomationIds cannot be declared in this
                 file at all — only injected from code-behind or smuggled through a
                 Style setter. This plan's own acceptance criterion counts the ids in
                 the XAML, and v6.0's `#export-dialog` likewise carries its own
                 `#export-cancel` / `#export-start` buttons inside the dialog element.
                 Esc still dismisses (ContentDialog returns `None`, which this file's
                 code-behind treats exactly like Cancel). -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                        Spacing="10">
                <Button x:Name="CancelButton"
                        Content="Cancel"
                        Style="{StaticResource DialogOutlinedButtonStyle}"
                        Click="OnCancelClick"
                        AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Cancel"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel" />
                <Button x:Name="ConfirmButton"
                        Content="Export"
                        Style="{StaticResource DialogAccentButtonStyle}"
                        Click="OnConfirmClick"
                        AutomationProperties.AutomationId="Export.Dialog.Confirm"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Export" />
            </StackPanel>
        </StackPanel>
    </Border>
</ContentDialog>
